  "body": "Measured on Windows in the build worktree of the coordinator session, 2026-11-21.\n\n- `target/debug/build/camcraft-app/` holds 3124 unit directories (`<hash>/out`) and 191 GB. Each `out/` holds a `libcamcraft_app-<hash>.rlib` (about 170 MB) and a `.pdb` (about 120 MB).\n- Each run of `cargo xtask gate quick` or `batch` adds about 600 to 645 new `camcraft-app` hashes. `camcraft-motion`, `camcraft-post` and `camcraft-sim` also get about 100 new units each run.\n- One quick gate wrote about 45 GB in 10 minutes. The disk fell from 79 GB to 7 GB free, and the gate had to be stopped at 14 GB free. Two runs failed with \"unable to copy .o (os error 2)\", most likely from the full disk.\n- `xtask/src/seed.rs` (#3117) does not cause this: it copies only units of packages without a source, and the `camcraft-app` units date from before #3117 merged.\n\nExpected: a gate run reuses the units of an earlier run when the code did not change, or at least removes the units that it replaces.\n\nWork:\n1. Find why each gate run, or each lane or step, gives `camcraft-app` a new unit hash (for example different `RUSTFLAGS`, features or profiles per step, or the layout of the build directory).\n2. Make the gate reuse the units, or remove the stale units of the earlier run.\n3. Add a check that a second gate run on the same tree adds no new units.\n",
